---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Social Media Manager Privacy Policy"
  description="How Velvet & Pixel’s Social Media Manager handles hosted media, workspace information, AI caption suggestions, social account connections and deletion."
>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy / Social Media Manager</p>
    <h1>
      Privacy Policy — <em>Social Media Manager</em>
    </h1>
    <p>
      <strong>Effective date:</strong> November 17, 2026
      <br />
      <strong>Developer/operator:</strong> Velvet &amp; Pixel
      <br />
      <strong>Contact:</strong>{" "}
      <a href="mailto:velvetandpixel@gmail.com">velvetandpixel@gmail.com</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      Social Media Manager is the working product name for Velvet &amp; Pixel’s
      Social HQ. This policy describes the current private pilot. It will be
      updated if the product name or data handling changes.
    </p>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      Social Media Manager is the working name for a Velvet &amp; Pixel tool for
      organizing business media, preparing captions, planning posts, reviewing
      content, and managing supported social-media connections. The current
      version is a private pilot. Availability of account connections and direct
      publishing depends on configuration, platform permissions, and enabled
      features.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is a hosted web application. Media and workspace information are sent
      to its hosting services; they are not stored only on your device.
    </p>
    <h2>Information processed</h2>
    <p>
      Workspace content includes photos and business logos you upload; file
      names, checksums and media metadata; photo notes; collection and category
      information; business facts, writing examples and brand preferences;
      captions, drafts, campaigns, schedules, approvals and publishing settings.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you authorize a supported social connection, the app processes
      authorization codes and access tokens, the identities and names of
      selected Pages or professional accounts, granted permissions, connection
      status and available social-platform information. This can include post
      identifiers, publishing outcomes, and available account or post
      performance metrics used by the app.
    </p>
    <p>
      The service also keeps operational information such as job status,
      activity history, delivery attempts, errors, timestamps, and AI request
      and usage records. Hosting and authentication providers may process
      technical information, such as IP addresses and request or device
      information, to operate and protect their services.
    </p>
    <p>
      Upload or enter only information you are authorized to use. Photos, notes
      and captions can contain personal information about customers or other
      people.
    </p>
    <h2>How information is used</h2>
    <p>
      Information is used to maintain your media library and workspace, prepare
      and review content, plan schedules, provide optional caption suggestions,
      connect selected accounts, carry out enabled publishing or manual-handoff
      workflows, display relevant account information, and diagnose or recover
      failed operations.
    </p>
    <p>
      AI suggestions do not themselves approve or publish a post. Approved
      scheduled work may later be processed without the browser remaining open
      where the relevant automation is enabled. Pausing, editing or deleting
      content cannot reliably recall a request already sent to an external
      service.
    </p>
    <h2>Hosting, storage and authentication</h2>
    <p>
      The current private pilot uses Cloudflare Workers, D1 and private R2
      storage for application processing, workspace records and media. Access to
      the private pilot is controlled through its ChatGPT-hosted access
      mechanism. These service providers process information under their
      applicable terms and privacy policies.
    </p>
    <p>
      Uploaded originals can retain embedded metadata, including location
      information. Generated publication images and thumbnails are re-encoded to
      remove EXIF/GPS and text metadata. Do not assume that an original upload
      has had its metadata removed.
    </p>
    <p>
      Business information, drafts, schedules, operational history and media may
      remain stored when you close the browser or sign out. Removing the web app
      or clearing browser storage does not delete the hosted workspace.
    </p>
    <h2>Optional AI caption suggestions</h2>
    <p>
      If enabled, caption generation sends text context to OpenAI. Context can
      include photo notes, saved business and brand facts, writing style,
      category information, campaign instructions, destination platforms and
      recent approved captions. Generated suggestions and related usage records
      are stored so you can review them and the service can manage requests and
      budgets.
    </p>
    <p>
      The current caption feature does not send uploaded photos for visual
      analysis. Text notes can still contain personal information; review them
      before requesting suggestions. The manual media and caption workflows can
      be used without AI.
    </p>
    <p>
      OpenAI may process request content and technical or usage information
      under the applicable API terms, privacy policies and account settings.
      Provider retention and data-use settings depend on the applicable account
      configuration and terms. Turning AI off does not recall a request already
      sent or automatically delete previously saved suggestions.
    </p>
    <h2>Facebook, Instagram and other external services</h2>
    <p>
      When you choose to connect a supported account, authorization takes place
      through the relevant platform. The app uses the authorization information
      to access permitted account details and perform enabled functions for the
      selected destination. It does not need you to enter your Facebook or
      Instagram password into Social Media Manager itself.
    </p>
    <p>
      For enabled direct publishing, the selected media, captions and related
      publishing information are transmitted to Meta. Where a platform needs to
      retrieve publication media, access may be provided through a time-limited
      media URL. If you use manual handoff instead, material you copy, download
      or upload to another service is handled under that service’s policies.
    </p>
    <p>
      Meta controls its own collection, use, retention and disclosure of
      information. Content you publish may be visible to the audience configured
      on that platform. Platform availability, approvals and connection status
      should not be interpreted as a guarantee that every advertised integration
      is operational.
    </p>
    <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
    <p>
      The app uses necessary browser mechanisms for authentication, connection
      security and workflow continuity. Meta authorization uses short-lived
      secure, HttpOnly cookies to match a connection attempt to the initiating
      browser; the current connection cookies expire after approximately ten
      minutes or are cleared when handled.
    </p>
    <p>
      Browser state can also support interrupted uploads and interface
      operation. The hosting and sign-in layer may use its own necessary cookies
      or session mechanisms under its policies. This document does not make a
      blanket “no cookies” claim.
    </p>
    <h2>Retention, deletion and disconnecting accounts</h2>
    <p>
      Workspace content and operational records are retained to support the
      library, review, scheduling, duplicate prevention and recovery workflows.
      A complete retention schedule has not yet been established for the private
      pilot. Contact{" "}
      <a href="mailto:velvetandpixel@gmail.com">velvetandpixel@gmail.com</a> to
      request deletion of hosted workspace information.
    </p>
    <p>
      Moving media to Trash prevents future selection and can cancel affected
      work that has not been dispatched. Removing stored media bytes is a
      separate background operation. In-flight operations may finish, and
      deletion may not be immediate. Some metadata, immutable approval or
      delivery records, and audit tombstones may remain for operational history
      and recovery. Earlier copies may also remain in exports, logs or backups
      where those exist.
    </p>
    <p>
      Disconnecting a platform removes the app’s saved connection, cancels
      relevant pending connection work and pauses publishing. To revoke the
      underlying authorization completely, also remove the integration in the
      platform’s own account settings. Disconnecting is not the same as deleting
      your whole workspace.
    </p>
    <p>
      Deleting library media, disconnecting an account or deleting a workspace
      does not automatically delete posts already scheduled or published on
      Facebook, Instagram or another service. Manage those posts directly with
      that platform. Copies you exported or shared must be managed separately.
    </p>
    <p>
      External providers retain information according to their own policies and
      applicable requirements. We cannot promise that a local deletion action
      removes every provider-held record.
    </p>
    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      The implementation uses access controls, private media storage, encrypted
      stored social credentials, and secure connection mechanisms. Limited
      access to publication media may be granted when required for delivery. No
      software or hosting system can guarantee absolute security.
    </p>
    <p>
      The current pilot is restricted to an authorized owner. It has not been
      represented as a fully isolated multi-customer service. Keep account
      access secure and review content and destination accounts before
      authorizing publishing.
    </p>
    <h2>International processing and privacy requests</h2>
    <p>
      Cloudflare, OpenAI, Meta and the authentication or hosting layer may
      process information in countries other than your own, subject to their
      applicable service arrangements and policies.
    </p>
    <p>
      For questions about access, correction, deletion or other privacy
      requests, contact{" "}
      <a href="mailto:velvetandpixel@gmail.com">velvetandpixel@gmail.com</a>. We
      may need to confirm that a request relates to an account or workspace you
      control. Available rights and any applicable exceptions depend on your
      location and circumstances.
    </p>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      The service is intended for business social-media management and is not
      directed to children. Do not submit children’s personal information unless
      you have the necessary authority and permissions.
    </p>
    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      We may revise this policy when the product name, functionality,
      integrations or data handling changes. The published policy will show its
      effective date.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
